<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes)",
        "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 53.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-bressloff-audit) and the assessments." ;
    schema:about "Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Fifth-order resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy (Bressloff 2001 Section 5.2), a validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream), or any comparison with psychophysical or anatomical measurements",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling, even/odd orientation eigenbranches and marginal-stability scans, cubic amplitude-equation coefficients gamma_0, gamma_3(theta), eta_hex and branch selection, log-polar pullback rendering of four form-constant presets, a Gaussian-only negative control, and an overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries vendored from the upstream MesmerPrism fixture",
        "reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even (contoured) and odd (non-contoured) planforms, pulled back through the log-polar retino-cortical map, give Klüver's four form constants",
        "reported_in_source: Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map",
        "reported_in_source: Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number",
        "transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to ~1e-15 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/bressloff_v1_metrics.csv; output: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png; organism: Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/68c4a1a; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; artifact_sha256: 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bressloff/driven-neural-fields-registry.json=4f07b5175a48bcb5..., datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json=af12b2c1aa3e38fa..., datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json=5e349c7b80185de4...}; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even (contoured) and odd (non-contoured) planforms, pulled back through the log-polar retino-cortical map, give Klüver's four form constants | Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map | Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number; reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling, even/odd orientation eigenbranches and marginal-stability scans, cubic amplitude-equation coefficients gamma_0, gamma_3(theta), eta_hex and branch selection, log-polar pullback rendering of four form-constant presets, a Gaussian-only negative control, and an overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries vendored from the upstream MesmerPrism fixture; transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to ~1e-15 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; does_not_claim: Fifth-order resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy (Bressloff 2001 Section 5.2), a validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream), or any comparison with psychophysical or anatomical measurements]; other sources: bressloff-v1-form-constants: reference implementation and calibration reports (commit 344863a) <https://github.com/MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-5> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking Neural-Field Bifurcation & Log-Polar Retino-Cortical Geometry" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 5.3e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Code-to-model traceability: 60/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Core functions carry docstrings naming the paper location (Eq. 3.12 local harmonics, Eq. 4.9 lateral harmonics, Section 4 / Figs. 16-17 dispersion, Eq. 5.14-5.15 gamma_2 / gamma_3, Section 2 / Eq. 2.1 pullback), presets are named by figure, and the figure panels are labelled with the figures they emulate. -12: branch_selection_for and _make_branch_candidate introduce a scoring functional (mode_count * (lambda A^2/2 + |eta| A^3/3 - denom A^4/4)) and a lattice-local fallback that have no cited equation. -8: planform_modes hard-codes phase scales 0.35, -0.25, 0.5 and -pi/2 offsets with no reference. -8: the clips to +-1.5 on eigenfunction coefficients, safe_denominator, wave_count = 12, sharpness = 2.1 and the tanh rendering nonlinearity are untraced numerical choices. -6: the contoured max-over-phi rendering (lines 729-742) is not tied to the papers' double-map construction, and the calibration-report-to-preset mapping (fig37 -> fig17_even, etc.) is asserted without explanation. -6: the docstring's \"Eq. 3.12 / 4.9\" numbers could not be verified against the 2001 paper's numbering. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L309–L315: local harmonic docstring cites 2001 Eq. 3.12; lateral at 343-345 cites Eq. 4.9 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L309-L315>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L474–L512: _make_branch_candidate score functional has no equation reference <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L474-L512>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L660–L691: planform_modes phase scales 0.35, -0.25, 0.5 untraced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L660-L691>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L405–L421: np.clip(..., -1.5, 1.5) on perturbative coefficients not in the source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L405-L421>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Model fidelity to source: 55/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-3> ;
    rdfs:comment "The lateral coupling W_n^lat(q) = (-1)^n/2 [e^{-x} I_n(x) - I e^{-x'} I_n(x')] with x = xi^2 q^2/4 and the sin(2n theta0)/(2n theta0) spread factor, the local Gaussian-difference harmonics e^{-2n^2 xi^2}, the second-order dispersion relation lambda_pm = W_1 + beta(W0 +- W2) + beta^2 sum (...)^2/(W_1 - W_m), and the roll/lattice criterion 2 gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0 all match the 2001 paper as I know it, and the Fig. 38 numbers (gamma_0 = 0.3768, gamma_3(2pi/3) = 0.1869) agree with the Lean Section 14 instance. -12: the \"exact parity\" is against the Rust implementation's actual outputs, and the fixture's own fig40_odd_hex_bifurcation check (expected triangle, actual honeycomb, passed=false) is silently reported as [PASS] because the script compares only to rep[\"selected_*\"]. -8: branch_selection_for scopes selection to the preset's lattice, so identical gamma/q* produce \"hexagonal\" for fig38 and \"rhombic\" for rhombic_stability_angle; the selected family is an input, not a model prediction. -7: for every non-auto preset the rendered wavenumber is 2 pi wave_count / extent rather than the critical q*, so the cortical wavelength never comes from the marginal-stability curve. -6: the pullback uses the asymptotic r_R = (w0/eps) exp(eps x/alpha) instead of Eq. 2.1's x = (alpha/eps) ln(1 + eps r/w0), y = beta r theta/(w0 + eps r), which introduces an artificial foveal singularity that has to be masked. -6: ad-hoc regularisers not in the paper (coefficient clips to +-1.5, safe_denominator, a max-over-phi scalar field standing in for the oriented-segment double map). -6: the m = 0 normalisation of the second-order term and the alpha = 3/pi, beta = 1.589/2 constants are taken from the Rust code and cannot be checked against a cited equation. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L343–L358: Fourier-Bessel lateral harmonic with (-1)^n sign, exp(-x) I_n(x) and spread factor matches 2001 Section 4 form <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L343-L358>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L835–L857: parity loop compares to rep['selected_pattern'] (Rust actual), never to rep['checks'] where fig40 expected 'triangle' and passed=false <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L835-L857>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L557–L587: lattice-local scoping makes selected_family depend on preset pattern; fig38 and rhombic_stability_angle CSV rows have identical gamma/q* but different selections <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L557-L587>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L747–L761: far-field log-polar asymptote with r_min clamp instead of Eq. 2.1; wave_number from wave_count at 638-642, not q* <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L747-L761>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphometric validation: 22/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "spectral_ring_metrics computes k*, wavelength, ring sharpness and azimuthal m2/m4/m6 harmonics on the cortical fields and writes them to the CSV, and the Gaussian-only control is a quantitative model-level check. -25: none of these numbers is compared with a value measured on a specimen or reported in the literature (no hypercolumn spacing in mm, no ring spacing in degrees of visual angle, no Klüver/Rule psychophysical statistic). -15: k* equals the preset's wave_count (12, 14, 24) by construction and the self-test threshold k* >= 6 is trivially met, so the metric validates the renderer's input, not the model. -12: the CSV's max(m4, m6) column is 0.95-0.99 for every preset including pure rolls (a single roll has |c_m| = 1 for all m), so the lattice-symmetry discriminator does not discriminate. -14: the one metric that does compare against a digitised paper figure, the Floquet source-curve RMS (0.154) in rule-2011-floquet.json, is read into floquet_overlap_rms but never printed or plotted, and upstream marks it outside threshold; the metrics are computed on the cortical sheet only, never on the retinal pullback that is the actual claimed form constant. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L769–L812: spectral metrics computed on cortical field; no reference values anywhere <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L769-L812>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1316–L1321: self-test only requires k* >= 6; k* is wave_count by construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1316-L1321>; bressloff_v1_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): kluver rows: k* = 14/12/12/24 = wave_count; m4_m6 column 0.954-0.986 for rolls and lattices alike — bressloff_v1_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 68c4a1a, text/csv, 1508 B, artifact_sha256 2b6efe3a19972d59918b8fd9d2000a5eee12b9093a7cf407e1fa5171f0324294 (sha256 2b6efe3a19972d59918b8fd9d2000a5eee12b9093a7cf407e1fa5171f0324294), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1194–L1196: floquet_overlap_rms read from fixture but never surfaced; upstream fit_objective has calibration_claim_allowed=false <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1194-L1196>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): bressloff-v1-form-constants stability_reports parity, max |Δ| = 0.0 dimensionless (reference 0.0, MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants commit 344863a1bd9e8a8e8c9cb20aced2897f3ffb2c4c) [maximum absolute error across all 5 Bressloff (2001) stability_reports (q*, λ*, γ(0), γ(θ), η_hex) vs paper-calibration.json]; Mexican-hat lateral inhibition critical wavenumber q* (Bressloff 2001 Fig. 16) = 1.028 dimensionless wavenumber (reference >0.5 (finite Turing/Euclidean symmetry-breaking wavelength), Bressloff et al. 2001 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 356:299 Fig. 16) [maximizer of max(λ_even(q), λ_odd(q)) with lateral_inhibition = 0.27] — interior peak prominence = 0.1200; Gaussian-only negative control critical wavenumber q* (lateral_inhibition = 0) = 0.05 dimensionless wavenumber (reference 0.05, q_min boundary of [0.05, 3.0] grid (monotonically decaying dispersion, prominence = 0.0)) [maximizer of λ(q) when Mexican-hat surround inhibition is removed (lateral_inhibition = 0.0)] — interior peak prominence = 0.00e+00; Klüver Tunnel/Rings cortical planform spectral ring sharpness = 30.556 ratio (peak/median PSD) (reference >5.0, Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 7 / Klüver 1966 Tunnel form constant) [2D FFT radial power spectrum peak/median ratio at k* = 14 cycles]; Klüver Honeycomb/Hex cortical planform spectral ring wavenumber k* = 24.0 cycles / domain (reference >0, Bressloff et al. 2001 Fig. 35 / Klüver 1966 Honeycomb form constant) [dominant radial FFT wavenumber of the 3-mode hexagonal cortical planform] — ring sharpness = 7.76." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-5> ;
    pk:hasProbability 2.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — MorphoEval overall 53.0/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The script is a careful, fully deterministic Python port of the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust formalism: Fourier-Bessel lateral harmonics with the (-1)^n sign and sin(2n theta0)/(2n theta0) anisotropy factor, Gaussian-difference local harmonics, the second-order perturbative dispersion relation, cubic gamma_3(theta) coefficients and the 2*gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0 roll-stability test all have the published structure, and the PNG, CSV and GIF regenerate byte-for-byte from SHA-pinned fixtures. Its headline \"exact parity to 1e-16\" is parity with another implementation's reported numbers, not with Bressloff et al.; the vendored fixture itself records that the Fig. 40 odd-hex case selects \"honeycomb\" where the paper expects \"triangle\", and the script prints [PASS] for it. The rendered form constants are chosen by preset (pattern, wave_count) rather than by the amplitude equations or the critical wavenumber, the retino-cortical map is the far-field asymptote rather than Eq. 2.1, and the Rule (2011) panel plots upstream Floquet boundaries whose own fit report says calibration_claim_allowed=false. Tunnel and spiral pullbacks look like Klüver/Bressloff figures; the honeycomb is a dot lattice, the GIF's cobweb/honeycomb frames are unrecognisable, and no morphometric is compared against any empirical or literature value. Overall 53.0/100 (faithfulness 44.0, reproducibility 74.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 68c4a1a; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 55, Morphological realism / specimen match 52, Parameter expressivity 35, Morphometric validation 22, Source and data traceability 72, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 85. Output judged: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 68c4a1a, image/png, 908688 B, 1972×1576 px, artifact_sha256 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514 (sha256 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; artifact_sha256: 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bressloff/driven-neural-fields-registry.json=4f07b5175a48bcb5..., datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json=af12b2c1aa3e38fa..., datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json=5e349c7b80185de4...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even (contoured) and odd (non-contoured) planforms, pulled back through the log-polar retino-cortical map, give Klüver's four form constants | Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map | Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number; reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling, even/odd orientation eigenbranches and marginal-stability scans, cubic amplitude-equation coefficients gamma_0, gamma_3(theta), eta_hex and branch selection, log-polar pullback rendering of four form-constant presets, a Gaussian-only negative control, and an overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries vendored from the upstream MesmerPrism fixture; transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to ~1e-15 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; does_not_claim: Fifth-order resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy (Bressloff 2001 Section 5.2), a validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream), or any comparison with psychophysical or anatomical measurements." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1123-1171 titles the panel 'Rule et al. (2011) Fig. 8 Floquet Tongues' although datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json fit_objective has calibration_claim_allowed=false, acceptance_status='outside-threshold-diagnostic' and note 'not a final published-figure reproduction'; floquet_overlap_rms (0.154) is returned at line 1194 but never printed or drawn. Show the RMS and the upstream status on the panel, and vendor the referenced source-curves file or drop the Fig. 8 claim.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1227-1230 make_gif overrides every preset to contour_mode='noncontoured', wave_count=3.5, sharpness=1.6; the resulting frames 3/4 and 4/4 (docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif) show four lobes and three blobs that do not resemble a cobweb or honeycomb; animate the same presets as the PNG or raise wave_count to an integer >= 8.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:28 gives Rule 2011 PMID 21980279 while datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib:54 gives 21980269, and paper_citations.bib:36 sets year=2001 for Ermentrout & Cowan 1979; line 69 imports scipy.special.iv as bessel_iv but never uses it (the script has its own series at 325-340), making scipy a spurious hard dependency.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:557-587 lattice-local scoping in branch_selection_for makes selected_family a function of the preset's pattern: CSV rows fig38_even_hex_bifurcation and rhombic_stability_angle have identical q*=1.447468, gamma0=0.376848, gamma_hex=0.186897 but report 'hexagonal' vs 'rhombic'. Report global_selected_family (and the stability booleans) in the CSV and figure so selection is a model prediction, not an input.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:638-642 for every non-auto preset wave_number = 2*pi*wave_count/(n*cell_mm), so the rendered cortical wavelength and the k*=12/14/24 'metrics' are preset inputs, not the critical q* from stability_scan; derive wave_number from critical_q/hypercolumn_mm (or document that the render is illustrative).",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:747-761 implements the far-field asymptote r_R=(w0/eps)exp(eps x/alpha) instead of Bressloff 2001 Section 2 / 2002 Eq. 2.1 x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r), creating an artificial foveal hole r<r_min; and the wavevector's y-component is not quantised to integer cycles over 2*pi*beta/eps (lines 670, 1229 with wave_count=3.5), which produces the visible seam along theta=+-pi in the spiral pullback of the PNG and GIF.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:794-801 and :1004 the azimuthal m4/m6 'lattice discriminator' written to bressloff_v1_metrics.csv is 0.954-0.986 for all four presets including pure rolls, because a single roll has |c_m|=1 for every m; normalise against m2 or use a ratio so the metric actually separates roll/square/hex, and compute it on the retinal pullback too.",
        "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:835-857 verify_paper_calibration_parity compares only to rep['selected_family']/rep['selected_pattern'] (the Rust implementation's actual output) and ignores rep['checks']; datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json records for fig40_odd_hex_bifurcation expected 'triangle' vs actual 'honeycomb' with passed=false, yet the self-test prints [PASS]. Surface the upstream checks and fail or flag when the paper expectation is not met.",
        "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:701-706,999-1000,1048 — For non-auto gallery presets (such as fig7_lattice_tunnel and fig31_square_even), render_cortical_and_retinal_planform renders the hardcoded params.pattern ('rings' or 'cobweb') while the retinal subplot title and CSV export report branch_selection['selected_pattern'] ('spiral'), mislabeling cols 1 and 3 of the middle row as mode=spiral.",
        "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:729-742,1227-1230 — Contoured cortical/retinal planforms collapse the orientation dimension via a scalar max-over-orientation tanh envelope rather than rendering Bressloff et al.'s (2001 Figs. 31-36) double-map local orientation contours, and make_gif overrides contour_mode='noncontoured' plus fixed pattern_angle_deg despite a comment claiming a continuous angle sweep.",
        "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:793-812,1004 — spectral_ring_metrics computes raw even azimuthal Fourier harmonics (c2, c4, c6) on the cortical grid and exports max(c4, c6) to bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, which evaluates to 0.9862 and 0.9815 for 1D roll gratings (fig7_lattice_tunnel, fig33_rhombic_even_roll) because a 1D stripe grating has all even azimuthal harmonics near 1.0." ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Parameter expressivity: 35/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The figure demonstrates two binary contrasts that are genuinely model-controlled: theta0 = 0 vs 60 degrees flips the critical branch from odd to even (Panel A), and lateral_inhibition 1 vs 0 removes the interior wavenumber peak (negative control). -20: no morphospace parameter is swept across a range; pattern_angle_deg (spiral pitch), eigen_beta, lateral_wide_sigma, lateral_spread_deg and wave_count each take one or two fixed values, so monotonic control of a feature of form is never shown. -15: the only continuously varied quantity (phase in the GIF) is a translation, not a morphospace coordinate. -15: the parameters that actually decide the rendered form (pattern, wave_count, pattern_angle_deg) are preset labels that bypass the model, while the model-driven quantities (q*, selected branch) do not change what is drawn unless pattern == \"auto\", which no gallery preset uses. -15: BressloffParams exposes 19 fields but there are no CLI flags to vary any of them, so a user cannot explore the morphospace without editing source. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L943–L950: only two spread values (0, 60 deg) and one inhibition toggle are ever contrasted <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L943-L950>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L700–L706: branch selection only affects rendering when pattern == 'auto'; all four gallery presets have fixed patterns <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L700-L706>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1326–L1332: CLI exposes only --out/--csv/--gif/--no-show/--self-test; no model parameter is settable <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1326-L1332>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Reproducibility package: 85/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Re-running `--no-show --out --csv --gif` reproduced the committed PNG, CSV and GIF byte-for-byte (SHA-256 73edc6ae..., 2b6efe3a..., df4acc7a...), the pipeline uses no RNG so no seed is needed, requirements.lock.txt pins exact versions with Python 3.14.7 / macOS arm64 and the venv matches (numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, pillow 12.0.0), fixtures are SHA-pinned and the run fails closed on mismatch, and `--self-test` passes in about 1.5 s. -5: the README section documents only `--gif PATH`; `--self-test`, `--no-show`, `--out` and `--csv` appear only in argparse. -4: `from scipy.special import iv as bessel_iv` is unused (the script has its own power series), so scipy is a spurious hard dependency. -3: the default `--gif` path is the repo root while the committed asset lives in docs/media, so the documented invocation does not regenerate the shipped file in place. -3: the README claims parity <= 6.7e-16 while the run reports 2.22e-16, a stale number that should be generated, not hand-written. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1326–L1343: argparse flags --out/--csv/--gif/--no-show/--self-test; outputs byte-identical on re-run <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1326-L1343>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L5: exact pip freeze with Python 3.14.7, macOS arm64, 2026-10-17 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L5>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L69–L69: unused scipy import bessel_iv <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L69-L69>; README.md L484–L488: documents only --gif PATH and claims <= 6.7e-16 parity <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/README.md#L484-L488>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Source and data traceability: 72/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "All four primary papers carry DOI and PMID in the docstring, the dataset README and the .bib; the upstream repository and its derivation chain are named with a full commit hash and MIT notice; the three JSON fixtures are SHA-256 pinned in the script and in datasets/bressloff/README.md with their upstream paths, and both GitHub URLs resolve. -8: the Rule et al. 2011 PMID differs between the script (21980279) and paper_citations.bib (21980269), so at least one identifier is wrong. -5: the .bib gives year = 2001 for Ermentrout & Cowan 1979. -8: the Floquet fixture's source_curve_comparison points to an upstream reports/source-curves file that is not vendored, so the digitised Fig. 8 curves the panel implicitly claims to reproduce cannot be inspected. -7: the retino-cortical constants alpha = 3/pi, beta = 1.589/2, w0 = 0.087, eps = 0.051 and the \"Eq. 3.12 / Eq. 4.9\" equation numbers are asserted without page or equation references that can be checked, and 11 of the 24 upstream runs carry status \"review\"/\"phase-selection-review\" that the script does not surface. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L11–L31: DOIs, PMIDs and pinned upstream commit 344863a1 in docstring <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L11-L31>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L74–L78: SHA-256 pins for the three vendored fixtures, verified at run time and fail-closed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L74-L78>; datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib L36–L54: Ermentrout & Cowan year=2001; Rule 2011 pmid=21980269 vs script's 21980279 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib#L36-L54>; datasets/bressloff/README.md L9–L13: fixture table with SHA-256 and upstream paths; source-curves file referenced by rule-2011-floquet.json not vendored <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/datasets/bressloff/README.md#L9-L13>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphological realism / specimen match: 52/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The tunnel (concentric rings) and spiral pullbacks in the PNG and GIF are convincing analogues of Klüver's tunnel and spiral families and of Bressloff et al.'s Fig. 31b/33b inverse maps, the four columns are visually distinct, and the cobweb pullback is a recognisable lattice of crossing log-spiral arcs. -10: nothing from a subject report or from Bressloff Fig. 1 / Ermentrout-Cowan 1979 is placed beside the output; the only reference is the paper's own model figures named in titles, and even those are not shown. -10: the honeycomb pullback is a lattice of isolated spots, not the hexagonal cells of Klüver's honeycomb or Fig. 35. -8: the GIF (the asset embedded in both READMEs) forces noncontoured mode with wave_count = 3.5, so frames 3/4 and 4/4 show four lobes and three blobs that no one would call a cobweb or a honeycomb. -6: the spiral panel has a visible seam along theta = +-pi because the wavevector's azimuthal component is not quantised to integer cycles over 2 pi beta/eps. -6: the funnel (radial rays) member of the tunnel/funnel family is never rendered and the cobweb column's retinal title reads \"mode=spiral\". -8: contoured planforms are drawn as a scalar max-over-orientation field rather than the oriented line segments the papers use, so the cobweb/honeycomb textures only loosely resemble the published double-map figures. Evidence: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): rings and spiral pullbacks recognisable; honeycomb pullback is a dot lattice; cobweb retinal title says mode=spiral; seam at theta=pi on left of spiral disc — bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 68c4a1a, image/png, 908688 B, 1972×1576 px, artifact_sha256 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514 (sha256 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif (generated output, not in repo): frames 3/4 and 4/4 show four lobes / three blobs, not cobweb or honeycomb; spiral frame has a horizontal seam — docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 68c4a1a, image/gif, 1498952 B, 640×340 px, 36 frames, artifact_sha256 df4acc7ae32e7ef54dcf2f78e982ae47357d3edbef3027a4a13b66d0bcecb018 (sha256 df4acc7ae32e7ef54dcf2f78e982ae47357d3edbef3027a4a13b66d0bcecb018), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1227–L1230: GIF overrides contour_mode=noncontoured, wave_count=3.5, sharpness=1.6 away from the paper presets <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1227-L1230>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L729–L742: contoured field is max-|val| over 16 orientation samples, not an oriented-segment double map <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L729-L742>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> a skos:Concept,
